      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test. The original has several unused imports and the `SYSTEM` check could be more readable with a clearer constant name and assertion message.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed all unused imports (serialization classes, `Arrays`, `ScratchBytes`, `ScratchChars`, and unused assertion methods), renamed `WINDOWS` to `IS_CASE_SENSITIVE_OS` with an explanatory comment to make the OS-sensitivity logic self-documenting, and added descriptive failure messages to each assertion so the intent is clear when a test fails."
